  "attemptNotes": {
    "red": "Initial frozen received-body API returned unavailable;0passed/1failed; stub/source/log retained.",
    "r2": "First frozen received-data roundtrip passes; native HTTP implementation added, before static-root refinement and expanded tests.",
    "r3": "13new contracts pass; one TLS fixture failed before receiving a request. Actual public HTTPS HTML/PDF capture and native PDF text separately pass on this source.",
    "r4": "Owned direct reqwest reproduction also failed with connection-aborted; production errors remain sanitized.",
    "r5": "Owned server event records Winsock10035 WouldBlock. Windows accepted sockets inherited the nonblocking listener mode.",
    "r6": "Explicitly blocking accepted sockets fixes the fixture; all14new cases pass. Runtime transport was not changed to relax TLS validation.",
    "quality": "Clippy required collapsing a nested charset if; input/source hashes retained.",
    "quality-r2": "All-target Clippy with warnings denied and format pass on final frozen source.",
    "final": "Final12selected groups516passed/1failed/8existingignored. Sole failure: unchanged media_cannot_bypass_source_scope_links_ignore_or_protected_paths actual Windows symlink setupOS1314. All14new tests pass. Attempts are nonadditive."
  },
  "notes": [
    "Rust owns one explicit public HTTP GET, frozen representation/body archive, exact byte ranges and separate native PDF-worker selection. No Graft/Serena/Graphify application wrapper or default model/project execution is added.",
    "Host-selected URL and literal SocketAddr fix the connection destination and TLS/HTTP name. Separate network/output/loopback grants are not deserializable from artifacts. No credential lookup, Authorization/Cookie forwarding, proxy, redirect, retry, script/resource/link fetching or query-time acquisition is performed.",
    "Public OS anchors are extracted explicitly; reqwest tls_certs_only selects offline WebPKI hostname/certificate verification. Host-added roots are bounded. New direct rustls-native-certs0.8.4 already existed transitively; the lock proof confirms all package versions, sources, checksums and unrelated dependencies remain unchanged.",
    "Received body bytes, Unicode/CRLF, base64 ranges, normalized selected header data and data-only capture claims retain their distinct precision. Split UTF8 ranges return null text and exact bytes. Metadata/source hashes are not server attestation, semantic identity or a canonical code snapshot. Imported claims cannot grant authority; complete remains false.",
    "HTML remains raw; article/browser DOM/social/video/semantic extraction is explicitly missing. Plain text is literal UTF8. Explicit frozen PDF text uses the installed native parser worker with existing byte/font/coverage/resource limits and no original asset path or Store.",
    "Actual Windows native capture/replay validates example.com HTML577bytes and W3dummyPDF13264bytes with matching body/archive hashes, native PDF text/page1, existing-output refusal and no source mutation. Owned lost-stdout HTTP preserves archive/hash identity. Public payload bytes remain in ignored local evidence; receipts/hashes and owned reproducible protocol/PDF fixtures are published here.",
    "Owned wire tests cover direct/chunked bodies, TLS custom roots and hostname failure, literal address override without DNS, separate host permissions, proxy isolation, redirects/status errors, duplicate content-type, compression, truncated bodies, quotas and cancel/deadline peer closure. These are labeled fixtures, not actual external backend certification.",
    "One direct export.arxiv.org API validation attempt timed out15s. A later direct public arxiv.org abstract-page investigation succeeds and finds citation metadata; neither is native arxiv implementation. Generic transport refuses arxiv domains including trailing-dot spelling until a dedicated rate-aware connector. No fake empty complete arxiv result is produced.",
    "Mandatory integrated typecheck/TypeScript260with3skips/Python17/format pass with695unchanged inputs. The media security test is unchanged and not skipped; OS1314 is retained. Selected evidence does not erase earlier whole-native/platform failures. Wider R7/R1–R9, arxiv/Google/social/video/database connectors, main and release remain open."
  ],
